<h1 id="colors">Colors and palettes</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">Choose colors by their role in your design. Text and background utilities are separate, so one palette can change the appearance of the same markup.</p>
<h2 id="color-utilities">Text and backgrounds</h2>
<p>Compare the primary and secondary text/background pairs side by side. Text color and background color each need their own class.</p>
{% set markup %}<div class="flex w-100">
  <div class="xs-w-50 py-40 flex items-center justify-center text-center fs-14 lh-20 clr-primary clr-primary-bg">
    <div>clr-primary<br>clr-primary-bg</div>
  </div>
  <div class="xs-w-50 py-40 flex items-center justify-center text-center fs-14 lh-20 clr-secondary clr-secondary-bg">
    <div>clr-secondary<br>clr-secondary-bg</div>
  </div>
</div>{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Primary and secondary color pairs") }}
<p><code>xs-w-50</code> gives each box half the width. Vertical padding supplies the box height while the flex utilities center the labels.</p>
<h2 id="buttons">Buttons</h2>
<p>Use <code>btn</code> for an inline-flex button with inherited typography, padding, a border, rounded corners, and a visible keyboard focus outline. Add <code>btn-primary</code> or <code>btn-secondary</code> to use the matching foreground and background palette values. The base button inherits text color and has a transparent background, so it can also be used inside a colored region.</p>
{% set markup %}<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-16 items-center">
  <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Primary button</button>
  <button class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Secondary button</button>
  <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Unavailable action</button>
  <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/docs/installation/">Installation guide</a>
</div>{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Primary and secondary buttons") }}
<p>These sample buttons demonstrate appearance; they do not run an action. Use a native <code>button</code> for actions and an anchor with a real destination for navigation. Native <code>disabled</code> prevents the unavailable button from activating; it also receives a dimmed appearance. Do not add <code>disabled</code> to an anchor.</p>
<p>Use existing spacing and layout utilities for variations, such as <code>btn btn-primary py-8 px-16</code>. Palette overrides flow through both button variants. Check text, borders, focus outlines, and disabled states against their actual surroundings when customizing colors; the named pairs do not guarantee accessible contrast for every palette.</p>
